blipster8 wrote:
> John H. wrote:
> > Sorry, I remembered the prior posts talking about using gnome healers
> > as a good option for pacifist challenge ascensions.
>
> Which is related to their being good at the protection racket: good
> starting HP (quaff some potions at the beginning), have gnomish
> infravision (to get them through the dark levels), etc.

They're less bad at the protection racket, but if you're going for a
first ascension it's not the right long-term strategy as has been
discussed here many times before--there's a reason you don't see
mrivan, anselmus, etc (people who are going for ascensions at a high
percentage, and have had 10 or more in a row without dying) doing
something as low-percentage as the racket (unless, of course, they're
trying a pacifist conduct ascension, but that's a whole other topic not
suited for newbies).

However, it is very valuable for a new player to play the racket a few
times to get used to running away, letting the pet fight, writing
Elbereth, etc.  It forces you to learn a bunch of tactics you might not
use otherwise.

Just don't fall in love with it, once you've done it a few times and
gotten the learning value from it, switch to more successful tactics
for general gameplay.



